<title>ITALY: Italian banks' bad loans increase - ABI.</title>
<headline>Italian banks' bad loans increase - ABI.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gross bad loans in the entire Italian banking system rose 15.4 percent year-on-year in May to 115.42 trillion lire after a 14.4 percent rise in April, provisional data from the Italian Banking Association ABI showed.</p>
<p>The ratio of bad loans to all loans, on a gross basis, rose to 10.86 percent from 10.70 percent in April. -- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
